{"step_index":256,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-17T14:52:27Z","thinking":"**Defining the Architecture**\n\nOkay, I'm now zeroing in on the System Design Document, specifically the `design.md` file. I've pinpointed that the user is requesting a GCP-centric architectural blueprint. The focus is to articulate the architecture and map the full solution based on the user's requirements.\n\n\n**Mapping the System Components**\n\nI'm now detailing the system components within the Google Cloud ecosystem. The breakdown includes: the client-side technologies, such as Cloud Run, Cloud Storage with Cloud CDN or Firebase Hosting for the Web Chat UI; and SSE or WebSocket streaming through Cloud Run. The ingress, gateway, and auth tier leverages Google Cloud API Gateway or Apigee, plus Cloud Load Balancing and Cloud Armor. Finally, I'm mapping AI safety guardrails using Vertex AI Model Armor and Content Safety, along with Cloud DLP for security.\n\n\n**Detailing the Architecture Components**\n\nI'm now diving into the specifics of service accounts for least-privilege access across tiers. I'm also fleshing out the Agent Orchestrator, which could use Vertex AI Agent Builder, LangGraph, or Cloud Run/GKE. For foundation models, I'm leaning toward Gemini 1.5 Pro/Flash on Vertex AI, and Memorystore for Redis will handle session state. Moreover, for the Policy Knowledge Base, I'm planning to ingest documents via Cloud Storage with a Pub/Sub notification pipeline using Eventarc, Cloud Functions or Cloud Run. The documents will be processed via Document AI, with vector embeddings from the Vertex AI Text Embedding API, and the Vertex AI Vector Search for retrieval.\n\n\n**Integrating the Adapters**\n\nI've been working on integrating specific system adapters. Specifically, the WorkWeek HCM and ServiceImmediately ITSM adapters are being deployed as Cloud Run microservices. They're using VPC Access Connector for secure egress. Google Cloud Secret Manager will handle secrets and API keys, and I'm considering Envoy, Resilience4j, or a custom Go circuit breaker for resilience.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Managing Resilience and Queues**\n\nNow, I'm focusing on resilience, messaging, and asynchronous dead-letter queues. I'm leveraging Cloud Pub/Sub, specifically the `hr-ops-dlq-topic` for dead-letter queue events. An HR Operations Notification Cloud Function will subscribe to this and integrate with PagerDuty, Slack, or HRSD. I'm also planning to use Cloud Tasks for reliable asynchronous task execution and exponential backoff retry handling.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Establishing Observability and Auditing**\n\nFinally, I'm establishing the observability, governance, and audit logging components. The primary audit database will be Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL, with CMEK, IAM database authentication, and a private IP in the VPC. For monitoring and tracing, I'm using Cloud Logging, Cloud Monitoring, and Cloud Trace, considering OpenTelemetry or Sherlog for distributed tracing.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Comprehensive Google Cloud Platform (GCP) System Design Document (design.md) for the HR Agentic Solution (MVP 1).","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# System Design Document: HR Agentic Solution (GCP Architecture)\n\n**Document Version:** 2.0.0 (Google Cloud Platform Edition)  \n**Target Platform:** Google Cloud Platform (GCP)  \n**Target LLM:** Google Gemini 1.5 Pro / Flash via Vertex AI  \n**Authors:** Principal Systems Architect & Principal Product Manager  \n**Status:** Approved / Ready for Implementation  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary & GCP Architectural Principles\n\nThe **HR Agentic Solution** is an enterprise AI-driven virtual assistant deployed natively on **Google Cloud Platform (GCP)**. The platform orchestrates complex, multi-turn HR and IT self-service workflows across **WorkWeek (HCM)**, **ServiceImmediately (ITSM/HRSD)**, and internal policy repositories.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    User([Employee]) --> LB[Cloud Load Balancing + Cloud Armor]\n    LB --> Gateway[API Gateway / Cloud Run]\n    Gateway --> Guard[Vertex Model Armor & Cloud DLP]\n    Guard --> Orchestrator[Agent on Cloud Run / Vertex AI]\n    Orchestrator --> Gemini[Gemini 1.5 on Vertex AI]\n    Orchestrator --> VectorSearch[(Vertex AI Vector Search)]\n    Orchestrator --> Adapters[Adapters on Cloud Run]\n    Orchestrator --> DLQ[(Cloud Pub/Sub DLQ)]\n```\n\n### Core GCP Design Tenets\n\n1. **Serverless-First & Elastic Scale:** All compute workloads (Chat UI, API Gateway, Agent Orchestrator, Integration Adapters) run on **Cloud Run** with automated scale-to-zero and sub-second scale-up.\n2. **Managed Enterprise AI via Vertex AI:** Leveraging **Gemini 1.5 Pro/Flash** with structured function calling, **Vertex AI Vector Search** for sub-millisecond semantic retrieval, and **Vertex AI Model Armor** for prompt injection defense.\n3. **Zero-Trust Identity with Cloud KMS:** Ingress traffic passes through an **API Gateway Mock Identity Assertion Layer** that cryptographically signs JWT session claims (`X-Authenticated-User`) using asymmetric keys in **Cloud KMS**.\n4. **Data Privacy via Sensitive Data Protection (Cloud DLP):** Real-time inspection and automated tokenization/redaction of Sensitive Personally Identifiable Information (SPII) before logs are written to **Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL** and **Cloud Logging**.\n5. **Resilient Asynchronous Messaging:** Multi-system chained workflows implement forward failure escalation via **Cloud Pub/Sub** and **Cloud Tasks** into an **HR Operations Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. High-Level GCP Topology & Component Decomposition\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Client_Ingress [\"1. Client & Edge Ingress Tier\"]\n        Browser[\"Employee Browser\"]\n        CDN[\"Cloud CDN / Firebase Hosting\\n(React Web Chat UI)\"]\n        GCLB[\"Cloud Load Balancing\\n(External HTTPS / SSL Offloading)\"]\n        Armor[\"Cloud Armor\\n(WAF, DDoS & Rate Limiting)\"]\n        \n        Browser <--> CDN\n        Browser -->|HTTPS / WSS| GCLB\n        GCLB --> Armor\n    end\n\n    subgraph Edge_Security [\"2. Gateway & Identity Tier\"]\n        APIGW[\"API Gateway / Cloud Run Auth Proxy\\n(Enforces Rate Limits & Session Routing)\"]\n        KMS[\"Cloud KMS / Secret Manager\\n(JWT HMAC/RSA Signing Keys)\"]\n        \n        Armor --> APIGW\n        APIGW <--> KMS\n    end\n\n    subgraph AI_Safety_Tier [\"3. AI Governance & Safety Tier\"]\n        ModelArmor[\"Vertex AI Model Armor\\n(Prompt Injection & Jailbreak Defense < 300ms)\"]\n        CloudDLP[\"Sensitive Data Protection (Cloud DLP)\\n(Automated SPII Redaction Engine)\"]\n        \n        APIGW --> ModelArmor\n    end\n\n    subgraph Agent_Core_GCP [\"4. Agent Orchestration Platform\"]\n        Orchestrator[\"Agent Orchestrator on Cloud Run\\n(LangGraph / Python Framework)\"]\n        Redis[\"Memorystore for Redis\\n(Session Context: 30m Inactivity TTL)\"]\n        Gemini[\"Vertex AI Gemini 1.5 Pro / Flash\\n(NLU, Reasoning & Tool Dispatch)\"]\n        \n        ModelArmor -->|Sanitized Prompt| Orchestrator\n        Orchestrator <--> Redis\n        Orchestrator <--> Gemini\n    end\n\n    subgraph Storage_And_RAG [\"5. Knowledge Base & Vector Store\"]\n        GCS_Policies[(\"Cloud Storage (GCS)\\nHR Policy Documents\")]\n        Eventarc[\"Eventarc / Pub/Sub Trigger\"]\n        DocAI[\"Document AI & Semantic Chunker\"]\n        VertexEmbed[\"Vertex AI Embeddings\\n(text-embedding-005)\"]\n        VectorSearch[(\"Vertex AI Vector Search\\n(ScaNN Approximate Nearest Neighbor)\")]\n        \n        GCS_Policies --> Eventarc --> DocAI --> VertexEmbed --> VectorSearch\n        Orchestrator <-->|Vector Retrieval k=4, score >= 0.70| VectorSearch\n    end\n\n    subgraph Adapters_Tier [\"6. System Integration Adapters\"]\n        VPC[\"Serverless VPC Access Connector\"]\n        WW_Adapter[\"WorkWeek HCM Adapter (Cloud Run)\\n(Circuit Breaker & Idempotent REST)\"]\n        SI_Adapter[\"ServiceImmediately Adapter (Cloud Run)\\n(15m Deduplication & Status Engine)\"]\n        \n        Orchestrator --> VPC\n        VPC --> WW_Adapter\n        VPC --> SI_Adapter\n    end\n\n    subgraph External_Systems [\"7. Target Enterprise Sandboxes\"]\n        WorkWeek[(\"WorkWeek HCM Sandbox\")]\n        ServiceImmediately[(\"ServiceImmediately Sandbox\")]\n        \n        WW_Adapter <-->|HTTPS REST| WorkWeek\n        SI_Adapter <-->|HTTPS REST| ServiceImmediately\n    end\n\n    subgraph Observability_DLQ [\"8. Governance, Observability & Dead-Letter Queue\"]\n        PubSubDLQ[(\"Cloud Pub/Sub\\n(hr-ops-dead-letter-topic)\")]\n        CloudSQL[(\"Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL\\n(Encrypted Audit Events Store)\")]\n        CloudWatch[\"Cloud Logging & Cloud Trace\\n(OpenTelemetry Telemetry)\"]\n        \n        Orchestrator -.->|On Chained Step Failure| PubSubDLQ\n        Orchestrator --> CloudDLP --> CloudSQL\n        Orchestrator --> CloudWatch\n        Orchestrator -->|Streaming SSE Tokens| Browser\n    end\n\n    style Armor fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#ffc107,stroke-width:2px;\n    style ModelArmor fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#ffc107,stroke-width:2px;\n    style CloudDLP fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#ffc107,stroke-width:2px;\n    style PubSubDLQ fill:#ffebee,stroke:#f44336,stroke-width:2px;\n    style Gemini fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#03a9f4,stroke-width:2px;\n    style VectorSearch fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#4caf50,stroke-width:2px;\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. GCP Service Mapping Matrix\n\n| Functional Requirement | GCP Service / Resource | Architectural Rationale |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Edge Ingress & WAF** | **Cloud Load Balancing + Cloud Armor** | Global Anycast IP, managed SSL certificates, DDoS mitigation, and IP-based rate limiting. |\n| **API Gateway & Auth Proxy** | **Cloud Run + Cloud KMS** | Serverless ingress proxy validating test personas and signing `X-Authenticated-User` JWT headers with CMEK keys. |\n| **Session Cache & Memory** | **Memorystore for Redis** | In-memory key-value store with sub-millisecond latency for multi-turn session state with automated 30m TTL expiration. |\n| **LLM & Reasoning Engine** | **Vertex AI (Gemini 1.5 Pro / Flash)** | Enterprise-grade foundation models supporting structured function calling, JSON mode, and 1M+ token context windows. |\n| **Vector Database (RAG)** | **Vertex AI Vector Search** | Industry-leading vector retrieval engine using ScaNN algorithms, delivering $< 10\\text{ms}$ query latency at scale. |\n| **Policy Ingestion Pipeline** | **Cloud Storage + Eventarc + Document AI** | Automated ingestion pipeline: file upload in GCS triggers Eventarc, parses PDFs via Document AI, and indexes embeddings. |\n| **Safety & Threat Defense** | **Vertex AI Model Armor** | Managed real-time guardrail scanning prompts for prompt injection, jailbreaks, and sensitive data leakage ($< 300\\text{ms}$). |\n| **PII / SPII Masking** | **Sensitive Data Protection (Cloud DLP)** | Automated inspection and de-identification of SSNs, home addresses, phone numbers, and health data in log streams. |\n| **Integration Adapters** | **Cloud Run + Serverless VPC Access** | Isolated containerized microservices executing idempotent REST calls to WorkWeek and ServiceImmediately via private egress. |\n| **Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)** | **Cloud Pub/Sub + Cloud Tasks** | Durable, multi-region asynchronous event bus capturing partial orchestration failures for manual HR Operations triage. |\n| **Audit & Governance Store** | **Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL** | Managed relational database storing immutable audit logs with Customer Managed Encryption Keys (CMEK). |\n| **Telemetry & Observability**| **Cloud Logging + Cloud Monitoring + Cloud Trace** | Native APM and distributed tracing across Cloud Run, Vertex AI, and external REST adapter calls. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Architecture & Database Schemas\n\n```mermaid\nerDiagram\n    AUDIT_EVENTS {\n        uuid event_id PK\n        string trace_id\n        string session_id\n        string employee_id\n        string event_type\n        string action_name\n        string target_system\n        jsonb request_payload_redacted\n        jsonb response_payload_redacted\n        string status\n        timestamp created_at\n    }\n\n    DLQ_MESSAGES {\n        uuid message_id PK\n        string trace_id\n        string employee_id\n        string workflow_name\n        string primary_reference_id\n        string failed_step\n        jsonb error_payload\n        int retry_count\n        string state\n        timestamp published_at\n    }\n\n    VERTEX_VECTOR_INDEX {\n        string chunk_id PK\n        string document_id\n        string section_title\n        string deep_link_url\n        string document_hash\n        vector embedding_vector\n        text text_content\n        timestamp indexed_at\n    }\n\n    REDIS_SESSION {\n        string session_id PK\n        string employee_id\n        jsonb conversation_history\n        jsonb pending_confirmation\n        int ttl_seconds\n    }\n```\n\n### 4.1. PostgreSQL DDL on Cloud SQL (`audit_events`)\n```sql\nCREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS \"uuid-ossp\";\n\nCREATE TABLE audit_events (\n    event_id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),\n    trace_id VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL,\n    session_id VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL,\n    employee_id VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL,\n    event_type VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL, -- 'TOOL_EXECUTION', 'SAFETY_INTERCEPT_INPUT', 'HITL_CONFIRM'\n    action_name VARCHAR(64),\n    target_system VARCHAR(64),       -- 'WorkWeek', 'ServiceImmediately', 'PolicyRAG'\n    request_payload_redacted JSONB,  -- Scrubbed via Cloud DLP\n    response_payload_redacted JSONB, -- Scrubbed via Cloud DLP\n    status VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL,     -- 'SUCCESS', 'BLOCKED', 'FAILED', 'PARTIAL_SUCCESS'\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\nCREATE INDEX idx_audit_employee ON audit_events(employee_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_audit_trace ON audit_events(trace_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_audit_created ON audit_events(created_at DESC);\n```\n\n### 4.2. Cloud Pub/Sub Dead-Letter Queue Message Payload\n```json\n{\n  \"specversion\": \"1.0\",\n  \"type\": \"com.enterprise.hr.agent.dlq.event\",\n  \"source\": \"//cloudrun.googleapis.com/projects/hr-agent-prod/services/agent-orchestrator\",\n  \"id\": \"dlq-msg-9812-4819\",\n  \"time\": \"2026-08-17T14:50:00Z\",\n  \"datacontenttype\": \"application/json\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"trace_id\": \"tr-gcp-98127391-ab23\",\n    \"employee_id\": \"EMP-1042\",\n    \"workflow_name\": \"UC-2.2-MedicalLeave\",\n    \"primary_reference_id\": \"LOA-8821\",\n    \"successful_step\": \"WorkWeek_SubmitLeaveOfAbsence\",\n    \"failed_step\": \"ServiceImmediately_CreateITRoutingTicket\",\n    \"error_details\": {\n      \"http_status\": 503,\n      \"error_message\": \"Gateway Timeout from ServiceImmediately endpoint\",\n      \"retry_attempts\": 2\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sequence & Control Flow Specifications\n\n### 5.1. Policy Q&A RAG Retrieval Flow on Vertex AI\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Employee as Employee\n    participant UI as Web Chat UI (Cloud Run)\n    participant APIGW as API Gateway\n    participant Armor as Vertex Model Armor\n    participant Agent as Orchestrator (Cloud Run)\n    participant VectorSearch as Vertex AI Vector Search\n    participant Gemini as Gemini 1.5 on Vertex AI\n    participant DLP as Cloud DLP\n\n    Employee->>UI: \"What is the bereavement leave policy?\"\n    UI->>APIGW: POST /api/v1/chat/message (X-Authenticated-User JWT)\n    APIGW->>Armor: Scan Input Prompt (< 300ms)\n    Armor-->>APIGW: Clean & Safe\n    APIGW->>Agent: Forward Request (trace_id: tr-981)\n    Agent->>VectorSearch: FindNeighbors(embedding, k=4, filter=\"category='leave'\")\n    VectorSearch-->>Agent: Top Chunks (Score: 0.89) + Deep Link URLs\n    Agent->>Gemini: GenerateGroundedResponse(Prompt, Chunks, Instructions)\n    Gemini-->>Agent: Grounded Response + Structured Citations\n    Agent->>DLP: De-identify & Redact Output SPII\n    DLP-->>Agent: Clean Response\n    Agent-->>UI: Stream Tokens via Server-Sent Events (SSE)\n    UI-->>Employee: Display Answer with Clickable Citation: \"[Leave Policy 2026, Sec 3.4]\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5.2. Transactional Leave Booking with Human-in-the-Loop Confirmation\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Employee as Employee (Jane Doe)\n    participant UI as Web Chat UI\n    participant Agent as Orchestrator (Cloud Run)\n    participant Redis as Memorystore Redis\n    participant WW as WorkWeek Adapter (Cloud Run)\n    participant CoreWW as WorkWeek Sandbox\n\n    Employee->>UI: \"Book 2 days of vacation for Thursday and Friday\"\n    UI->>Agent: Dispatch Turn (JWT: EMP-1042)\n    Agent->>WW: getLeaveBalances(employee_id=\"EMP-1042\")\n    WW->>CoreWW: GET /balances (Real-Time)\n    CoreWW-->>WW: { vacation_remaining: 10.0 work days }\n    WW-->>Agent: 10.0 Days Available\n    Agent->>Agent: Calculate Business Days (2.0 Work Days, Exclude Holidays)\n    Agent->>Redis: Set pending_action(\"act-881\", { days: 2.0, type: \"Vacation\" })\n    Agent-->>UI: Render Confirmation Card (Dates: Sep 4-8, 2.0 Work Days)\n    \n    Note over Employee,UI: User Reviews Summary Card & Clicks [Confirm & Submit]\n    Employee->>UI: Clicks [Confirm & Submit]\n    UI->>Agent: POST /api/v1/actions/confirm (action_id=\"act-881\")\n    Agent->>Redis: Invalidate pending_action(\"act-881\")\n    Agent->>WW: submitLeave(Idempotency-Key: uuid-v5, Days: 2.0)\n    WW->>CoreWW: POST /leave_requests\n    CoreWW-->>WW: HTTP 201 Created (Ref: \"LV-4819\", Status: \"SUBMITTED_FOR_APPROVAL\")\n    WW-->>Agent: Success (Ref: \"LV-4819\")\n    Agent-->>UI: \"Your vacation request for 2.0 days has been submitted for manager approval (Ref: LV-4819).\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5.3. Chained Medical Leave with Cloud Pub/Sub DLQ Error Handling\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Employee as Employee\n    participant UI as Web Chat UI\n    participant Agent as Orchestrator (Cloud Run)\n    participant WW as WorkWeek Adapter\n    participant SI as ServiceImmediately Adapter\n    participant PubSub as Cloud Pub/Sub (DLQ Topic)\n    participant CloudSQL as Cloud SQL Audit DB\n\n    Employee->>UI: Confirm Medical Leave (5 Days)\n    UI->>Agent: Execute Chained Workflow (UC-2.2)\n    \n    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)\n        Note over Agent,WW: Step 1: WorkWeek Leave of Absence Submission\n        Agent->>WW: submitLeave(Type: LOA, Duration: 5.0)\n        WW-->>Agent: HTTP 201 Created (Ref: \"LOA-8821\")\n    end\n    \n    rect rgb(255, 235, 238)\n        Note over Agent,SI: Step 2: ServiceImmediately Notification Ticket\n        Agent->>SI: createTicket(Category: AccessRouting, Ref: \"LOA-8821\")\n        SI--xAgent: HTTP 503 Service Unavailable (After 2 Retries)\n    end\n    \n    rect rgb(255, 243, 224)\n        Note over Agent,PubSub: Step 3: Forward DLQ Event Publication\n        Agent->>Agent: Preserve WorkWeek State (Do NOT Rollback LOA-8821)\n        Agent->>PubSub: Publish Event to \"hr-ops-dlq-topic\" (LOA-8821, EMP-1042)\n        Agent->>CloudSQL: Log Audit Event (Status: \"PARTIAL_SUCCESS\")\n        Agent-->>UI: \"Your Leave has been recorded in WorkWeek (Ref: LOA-8821). However, the IT routing ticket timed out. HR Operations has been notified.\"\n    end\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Security, Compliance & Identity Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    subgraph Edge_Auth [\"1. Edge Authentication\"]\n        Request[\"Inbound HTTPS Request\"] --> ArmorCheck{\"Cloud Armor\\nRate Limits & WAF\"}\n        ArmorCheck -- Pass --> JWTCheck{\"Valid Signed\\nJWT?\"}\n        JWTCheck -- Valid --> ExtractClaims[\"Extract Claims\\n(sub, role, dept)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph RBAC_Gating [\"2. Orchestration RBAC Gating\"]\n        ExtractClaims --> InvariantCheck{\"caller_id ==\\ntarget_resource_id?\"}\n        InvariantCheck -- Mismatch --> Block403[\"HTTP 403 Access Denied\\n(Cross-User Block)\"]\n        InvariantCheck -- Match --> RouteTool[\"Dispatch to Adapters via VPC\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph DLP_Scrubbing [\"3. Cloud DLP Privacy Redaction\"]\n        RouteTool --> AdapterCall[\"Execute Adapter Call\"]\n        AdapterCall --> DLPInspection[\"Cloud DLP API Inspection\\nDe-identify SSN, Phone, Address, Health\"]\n        DLPInspection --> EncryptedLogs[(\"Cloud SQL Audit Log\\n(CMEK Encrypted)\")]\n    end\n\n    style ArmorCheck fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#ffc107;\n    style Block403 fill:#ffebee,stroke:#f44336;\n    style RouteTool fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#4caf50;\n    style EncryptedLogs fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#03a9f4;\n```\n\n### Security & Compliance Controls\n1. **Customer Managed Encryption Keys (CMEK):** All Cloud SQL instances, GCS buckets, Pub/Sub topics, and Cloud KMS key rings use dedicated Google Cloud KMS keys.\n2. **Workload Identity Federation & Least Privilege:** Cloud Run services communicate using dedicated service accounts (`sa-orchestrator@`, `sa-workweek-adapter@`, `sa-si-adapter@`) with minimal IAM bindings.\n3. **Data Loss Prevention (DLP):** Inspection rulesets automatically redact US/EU phone numbers, postal addresses, SSNs, and health markers from logging sinks.\n4. **GDPR DSR Support:** Cloud SQL audit logs older than 30 days are automatically pruned via Cloud Scheduler + Cloud Functions.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Non-Functional Specifications & Operational SLAs\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                              GCP LATENCY BUDGET & SLA MATRIX                           │\n├──────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Component / Request Type     │ Target Latency (p50)    │ Target Latency (p95)          │\n├──────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Cloud Armor + Edge Ingress   │ < 25 ms                 │ < 50 ms                       │\n│ Vertex Model Armor Scanning  │ < 100 ms                │ < 250 ms                      │\n│ Vertex AI Vector Search      │ < 15 ms                 │ < 40 ms                       │\n│ Gemini 1.5 Generation (SSE)  │ < 1.0 s (TTFT)          │ < 2.2 s                       │\n│ Policy Q&A RAG End-to-End    │ < 1.2 s                 │ < 2.8 s                       │\n│ Single-System Transactions   │ < 1.5 s                 │ < 3.5 s                       │\n│ Chained Workflows (UC-2.x)   │ < 3.5 s                 │ < 6.5 s                       │\n└──────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n* **Service Availability:** $99.9\\%$ SLA backed by multi-zone Cloud Run and High-Availability Cloud SQL.\n* **Throughput:** 50 concurrent active sessions; 5,000 monthly transactions in MVP 1.\n* **Disaster Recovery (DR):** Recovery Time Objective ($\\text{RTO}) \\le 15\\text{ minutes}$; Recovery Point Objective ($\\text{RPO}) \\le 5\\text{ minutes}$.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Infrastructure as Code (Terraform) Blueprint\n\n```hcl\n# Google Cloud Platform Baseline Architecture Terraform Blueprint\n\nterraform {\n  required_version = \">= 1.5.0\"\n  required_providers {\n    google = {\n      source  = \"hashicorp/google\"\n      version = \"~> 5.30.0\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n# 1. Cloud Storage Bucket for HR Policies\nresource \"google_storage_bucket\" \"hr_policies\" {\n  name                     = \"hr-agent-policies-prod-${var.project_id}\"\n  location                 = \"US\"\n  uniform_bucket_level_access = true\n  versioning {\n    enabled = true\n  }\n  encryption {\n    default_kms_key_name = google_kms_crypto_key.storage_key.id\n  }\n}\n\n# 2. Vertex AI Vector Search Index\nresource \"google_vertex_ai_index\" \"policy_vector_index\" {\n  region       = \"us-central1\"\n  display_name = \"hr-policy-vector-index\"\n  description  = \"ScaNN vector index for HR policy chunks\"\n  metadata {\n    config {\n      dimensions                  = 768\n      approximate_neighbors_count = 150\n      distance_measure_type       = \"COSINE_DISTANCE\"\n      algorithm_config {\n        tree_ah_config {\n          leaf_node_embedding_count    = 1000\n          leaf_nodes_to_search_percent = 10\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n# 3. Memorystore for Redis (Session Cache)\nresource \"google_redis_instance\" \"session_cache\" {\n  name           = \"hr-agent-session-cache\"\n  tier           = \"BASIC\"\n  memory_size_gb = 2\n  region         = \"us-central1\"\n  redis_version  = \"REDIS_7_0\"\n}\n\n# 4. Cloud Pub/Sub Topic for Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ)\nresource \"google_pubsub_topic\" \"hr_ops_dlq\" {\n  name = \"hr-ops-dead-letter-topic\"\n  kms_key_name = google_kms_crypto_key.pubsub_key.id\n}\n\n# 5. Cloud Run Agent Orchestrator Service\nresource \"google_cloud_run_v2_service\" \"agent_orchestrator\" {\n  name     = \"hr-agent-orchestrator\"\n  location = \"us-central1\"\n  ingress  = \"INGRESS_TRAFFIC_INTERNAL_LOAD_BALANCER\"\n\n  template {\n    containers {\n      image = \"gcr.io/${var.project_id}/agent-orchestrator:v1.0.0\"\n      resources {\n        limits = {\n          cpu    = \"2\"\n          memory = \"2Gi\"\n        }\n      }\n      env {\n        name  = \"PROJECT_ID\"\n        value = var.project_id\n      }\n      env {\n        name  = \"REDIS_HOST\"\n        value = google_redis_instance.session_cache.host\n      }\n      env {\n        name  = \"DLQ_TOPIC\"\n        value = google_pubsub_topic.hr_ops_dlq.name\n      }\n    }\n    scaling {\n      min_instance_count = 1\n      max_instance_count = 20\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n","Description":"Create GCP System Design Document design.md in artifact directory","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/usr/local/google/home/gauravrawat/.gemini/jetski/brain/ca4322d4-9341-4bd7-ad62-33640faaced0/design.md","toolAction":"Writing GCP design.md to artifact directory","toolSummary":"Write GCP design.md artifact"}}]}
